---
description: Semptify mandatory pre-flight and doc hierarchy for all AI assistants
alwaysApply: true
---

Before making any change in this repo, read in order:
1. `AGENTS.md` — Python 3.11.9 mandate, Known Failure Registry, module contract rules.
2. `ACTIVE_CONTEXT.md` — current priority. Do not start something else.
3. `BUILD_STATE.md` (last 2 entries) — what shipped, what is known broken/pending.
4. `PROJECT_BIBLE.md` — canonical doc hierarchy: BIBLE > README > AGENTS > SECURITY > DEPLOYMENT > BUILD_GUIDE.

Slash-command workflows for this repo are defined in `.devin/skills/*/SKILL.md` and mirrored
as VS Code prompt files in `.github/prompts/*.prompt.md` (`/preflight`, `/ship`, `/forge`,
`/review`, `/cloudflare-dev-mode`, `/help-page-review`, `/ssot-analysis`). Read the relevant
one before doing that kind of task. If you update a skill, update both copies.

State your plan (files to touch, why it won't repeat a Known Failure) before editing.
Verify changed Python files compile (`python -m py_compile <file>`) before ending the session.
